    "11": "Saul rescues Jabesh-Gilead from the Ammonites, earning support. He is confirmed as king at Gilgal.",
    "12": "Samuel gives his farewell address, reminding Israel of God's faithfulness and warning against disobedience.",
    "13": "Saul offers an unlawful sacrifice. Samuel rebukes him and says his kingdom won't endure.",
    "14": "Jonathan wins a battle with God's help. Saul makes a rash oath that nearly costs Jonathan's life.",
    "15": "Saul disobeys God by sparing Amalekite king and livestock. Samuel declares that God has rejected him as king.",
    "16": "Samuel anoints David, a young shepherd, as future king. The Spirit departs from Saul, and David enters his service.",
    "17": "David defeats Goliath with faith and a sling. Israel is encouraged and victorious.",
    "18": "David becomes a military leader and Saul's jealousy grows. Jonathan and David become close friends.",
    "19": "Saul tries to kill David, but Jonathan and Michal help him escape.",
    "20": "Jonathan confirms Saul’s intent to kill David. They make a covenant of friendship.",
    "21": "David flees, receiving holy bread and Goliath’s sword. He feigns madness before the king of Gath.",
    "22": "Saul kills priests who helped David. David's family and others join him at Adullam.",
    "23": "David saves Keilah but flees Saul. Jonathan strengthens him. Saul nearly catches David but is called away.",
    "24": "David spares Saul in a cave, proving his innocence. Saul acknowledges David's righteousness.",
    "25": "Abigail wisely prevents David from avenging Nabal. After Nabal dies, David marries her.",
    "26": "David again spares Saul at night, taking his spear and water jug.",
    "27": "David lives among the Philistines and gains favor by raiding enemies under false pretenses.",
    "28": "Saul consults a medium at Endor. Samuel's spirit appears and foretells Saul's death.",
    "29": "Philistine leaders reject David's participation in battle. He is sent back from the front.",
    "30": "Amalekites raid Ziklag. David pursues and recovers all. He shares the plunder generously.",
    "31": "Saul and his sons die in battle against the Philistines. Israel mourns their defeat."
